  <!--
    #8064 FR-023: the OPT-IN interactive test target.

    keybd_shift.interactive.tests.cpp injects real keyboard input and reads it back. It needs an
    interactive input desktop, and for two of its four tests a desktop that routes keyboard messages
    to a pumped, hooked message queue. A Session-0 CI service account has neither, which is why
    these tests are NOT in keyman32.tests.vcxproj and why build.sh exposes them as
    `test-interactive:x86` / `test-interactive:x64` rather than as part of the `test` action.

    In that file an absent capability is FAIL(), not SUCCEED(). That is only correct because this
    project is built and run deliberately, by a person, on a desktop where the capability is
    supposed to exist. Do not add it to the default target (FR-022, SC-005).

    Everything below is keyman32.tests.vcxproj with three differences: a different ProjectGuid, its
    own IntDir (so the two projects do not share pch.pch), and a single source file. The IntDir sits
    under obj\$(Platform)\ rather than beside it, so windows/src/.gitignore's **/obj/Win32/ and
    **/obj/x64/ rules cover this project's intermediates too.
  -->
